 mark, using a sorted table of grade boundaries","Finding the price for a plan code such as STD or PRE","Finding a student's form group from their student ID","Finding a product's name from its barcode number"],ans:0,explain:"With <b>TRUE</b> and the first column sorted smallest to largest, a mark of 67 falls back to the largest boundary not above it: <b>60, Merit</b>. Codes, IDs and barcodes need an exact match, so <b>FALSE</b>."},{sec:"bug",type:"mcq",prompt:'F2 contains <b>"STD "</b> (with a space at the end). What happens?',visual:()=>t("STD␣","#N/A",{F2:"look",G2:"bad"},{E14:"range"}),opts:["It still finds STD, because Excel ignores spaces at the end",'#N/A, because "STD " is not an exact match for "STD"',"#REF!, because the space pushes it outside the table range","It returns £9 but shows a small green warning triangle"],ans:1,explain:"An extra space counts as a character. This is why <b>cleaning your data</b> (e.g. with TRIM) matters in Task 2."}],teach:{meet:{title:"Your finger goes down, then across",blocks:[{p:"Picture VLOOKUP as your finger on the table. It goes <b>down</b> the first column until it finds the value, then <b>across</b> that row to the column you asked for."},{visual:t("STD",o,{F2:"look"},{E13:"scan",E14:"hit",F14:"ret"},{legend:[["#ffe1ee","1. what to look for"],["#fff0c2","2. scan down column E"],["#c9f7ee","3. match found"],["#e6dcff","4. move across, bring back"]]})},{tip:"The table must start with the column you are searching. VLOOKUP cannot look to the <b>left</b> of it."}]},read:{title:"Count columns from the edge of the table",blocks:[{p:"The column number counts from the <b>left edge of the table</b>, not from column A of the sheet. In <code>$E$13:$F$15</code>, E is column 1 and F is column 2."},{visual:{sheets:[n(h)],legend:[["#c9f7ee","column 1 (E), searched"],["#e6dcff","column 2 (F), brought back"]]}},{p:"Two errors to know for this round:"},{table:{rows:[["#N/A","The value was not found in column 1."],["#REF!","The column number is wider than the table."]]}},{tip:"The header row (Code, Price) is left out of the range on purpose. Start the table on the first row of real data."}]},eng:{title:"The sentence frame",blocks:[{p:"Every VLOOKUP can be read aloud with the same sentence. Learn the frame and you can translate any formula, in either direction."},{c:u,frame:["Look up the value in ",{text:"cell",c:f},", in the table on the ",{text:"sheet name",c:r}," sheet between ",{text:"first cell",c:r}," and ",{text:"last cell",c:r},", and give me whatever is in the ",{text:"Nth",c:u}," column of that table on the matching row. ",{text:"Must be an exact match.",c:F}]},{visual:{fx:"=VLOOKUP(B4, Prices!$A$2:$C$20, 3, FALSE)"}},{p:'"Look up the value in <b>B4</b>, in the table on the <b>Prices</b> sheet between <b>A2</b> and <b>C20</b>, and give me whatever is in the <b>3rd</b> column of that table on the matching row. <b>Must be an exact match.</b>"'},{tip:"The number is always a <b>column</b>, never a row. VLOOKUP finds the row for you."}]},typo:{title:"The syntax checklist",blocks:[{p:"When a formula breaks, check these in order. Most typos are one of these six."},{table:{rows:[["VLOOKUP","Spelt right? A misspelt function shows <b>#NAME?</b>"],[", , ,","Exactly <b>3 commas</b> separating 4 arguments."],["E13:F15","A <b>colon</b> between the first and last cell of a range."],["Analysis!","An <b>exclamation mark</b> after a sheet name."],["( )","Every opening bracket has a closing one."],['F2 not "F2"',"No quote marks around cell references. Quotes turn it into text."]]}},{tip:"Excel colours each cell reference in a formula and draws a matching box on the sheet. If the box is not where you expect, the reference is wrong."}]},dollar:{title:"Lock the table, not the lookup value",blocks:[{p:"When you fill a formula down, Excel moves every reference down a row, unless it has <b>$</b> signs. For VLOOKUP you want one part to move and one part to stay still."},{visual:{sheets:[{tab:"Data",cols:["F","G"],sta